Three new documents, no code (none of the laptop-owned progress docs is touched, so the next package merges cleanly):
- docs/MT_COMMAND_TABLE_machine.md: the machine's version of the W4 command table at C++ 7961939 / web a5454b9 -- 48 commands /
  37 actions, each with page source, C++ handler, layer (1203 / MOT / ui / refused), golden line, ctest coverage and what is still
  to verify on the machine; what each button does on this machine (8 buttons move a motor), the safety behaviours now active, and
  a risk-ordered on-machine checklist. Does not replace W4_PROGRESS.md.
- docs/MACHINE_GATES_OPENED_20260926.md: the W2 premise re-check record for the 19 gates opened in 0d253a0 (MT-E3b) and
  8929d13 (MT-FIX1b), done after the fact with nm on build_integ_ship_x86 objects; g2 G03 premise re-checked (stale; the laptop
  opened it in eed5033b); 10 still-closed candidates whose dependency now exists (h4-G4 among them, opened by the laptop 760c13d2).
- docs/ENGINE_1203_MOTOR_ROUTE_DESIGN.md: design for EastSun ruling 20260926 "甲" -- the engine's TMyEtherCatMotor (#else arm,
  ht9045_motor has no HAVE_PCI1203) reaches the card through TPci1203Control::Execute on the monitor's handle, like
  Pci1203IoRoute. Read-only draft; an adversarial critique found 5 high issues (setting writes counted as motion, MotorType vs
  motorClass numbering, no START_RING precondition, stop de-duplication, HOME energize+home in one tick) -- they are to be fixed
  in the implementation, together with EastSun's rulings of 20260926 (INDEX_MOTION_CARD effective 1 when the table puts MTestZ1
  on the 1203; DS402 coordinate writes refused; StopAllMotor stops every 1203 axis; EMG release re-energizes per golden but clears
  only the axis' own alarm; soft limits stay +-999999).

